-- Passage rg7-figurative-language-p01
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1f6d4ece-73f1-5f36-a628-23e0cc35acf1', 'rg7-figurative-language-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-figurative-language'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Last Lap$q$, $q$Kiona Redcloud stood at the starting line of the 1600-meter race, her heart a drum pounding in her chest. The stands were packed, and the noise rolled over the track like ocean waves. She had trained all summer for this moment.

When the starter's pistol cracked, the runners shot forward. Kiona settled into the middle of the pack. Her coach, Mr. Ostrowski, had told her again and again to save her energy for the final lap. "Be the tortoise early," he liked to say, "and the hare at the end."

By the third lap, her legs felt like they were filled with wet sand. The leader, a tall girl named Beatriz, was a gazelle, gliding smoothly ahead without any sign of strain. Kiona's lungs burned. Doubt whispered in her ear that she should slow down and be happy with fourth place.

Then the bell rang for the final lap. Kiona remembered her coach's words and let her arms pump faster. One runner fell behind her, then another. The gap between her and Beatriz shrank inch by inch.

Coming around the last curve, Kiona found a burst of speed she did not know she had. The finish line seemed to rush toward her. She crossed it a single step behind Beatriz, gasping for air.

Afterward, Beatriz walked over and shook her hand. "You came out of nowhere," she said, smiling. Kiona laughed. She had lost the race, but she had run the smartest race of her life, and that felt like a victory of its own.$q$, 'draft')
