  ('f3b9534c-bb9a-5757-922a-df87b0bf0521', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Some neighbors call Mr. Halvorsen "stubborn," but Tamika calls him "determined." What does Tamika's word choice show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She agrees completely with the neighbors who complained about him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-connotation"},{"text":"She thinks he is unwilling to listen to anyone else's ideas.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-connotation"},{"text":"She sees his refusal to quit as a good quality, not an annoying one.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She believes he is working too slowly to finish on time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She sees his refusal to quit as a good quality, not an annoying one.$q$, $q$Both words describe someone who will not give up, but "determined" has a positive feeling, and Tamika shows her approval by joining him. Being unwilling to listen matches the negative word "stubborn," which is the neighbors' view.$q$, 'draft', 'fcdfaa01-2c15-5899-b5f6-d27183a93eb3')
