   $q$The author says the waggle dance "is the hive's map and its news report rolled into one." What does this comparison suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The dance tells other bees both that food was found and where to go.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The dance is mainly a way for the bees to have fun together.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The bees draw pictures of flowers on the walls of the hive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The queen uses the dance to give orders to the worker bees.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The dance tells other bees both that food was found and where to go.$q$, $q$A news report shares that something happened, and a map gives directions; the dance tells bees about "a rich patch of flowers" and "where the flowers are." The queen giving orders contradicts the text, which says "she does not give commands."$q$, 'draft', '8cafda76-e587-5302-bd0a-4cd85cba334e')
