   $q$The author writes that "Every bridge has an Achilles' heel." Based on the passage, what does this allusion suggest about suspension bridges?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Even a very strong bridge can have one weak point that needs attention.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Most suspension bridges are weak overall and are likely to fail soon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Bridges are named after famous heroes who were known for their strength.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The bottom ends of the bridge, where it meets the ground, are the weakest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Even a very strong bridge can have one weak point that needs attention.$q$, $q$The author explains the phrase right away as "a single weak point" in a bridge that is otherwise "remarkably strong." Saying bridges are weak overall ignores the "single" weakness the allusion points to.$q$, 'draft', 'dd2590a3-c0e6-5a34-89a6-fa7468410075')
