   $q$Elijah "strolled to the podium as if he owned the room." What does this phrase suggest about him?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He was nervous and walked slowly to delay his turn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"He acted very relaxed and sure that he would win.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He was the student in charge of running the debate.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"His family owns the building where the school is.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He acted very relaxed and sure that he would win.$q$, $q$Acting "as if he owned the room" shows Elijah felt in control and very sure of himself, and "strolled" adds a relaxed feeling. Nothing suggests he was nervous; his loud, quick speech shows the opposite.$q$, 'draft', 'a13b98dc-7e03-5ab6-8a07-82bb3be47390')
