   $q$The narrator says Elijah's argument "was like the first little pig's house of straw." What does this allusion to the familiar folktale suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It was weakly built and fell apart as soon as it was challenged.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It was carefully built from facts that stood up to every question.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-allusion"},{"text":"It was the funniest argument, so the class enjoyed it the most.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It was mostly about farm animals and how they build their homes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It was weakly built and fell apart as soon as it was challenged.$q$, $q$The straw house falls easily, and the text adds, "One good puff, and it fell apart," right after Soo-ah corrected him. Being built from strong facts describes Soo-ah's points, "like bricks in a wall," not Elijah's.$q$, 'draft', 'a13b98dc-7e03-5ab6-8a07-82bb3be47390')
