   $q$In the fourth stanza, the repeated line changes to "Up the keys, and down, and again." Why does the poet make this change?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The change is a printing error, since the meaning of the line stays exactly the same.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-craft"},{"text":"The new commas show that the speaker is making more mistakes than on Wednesday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"The change shows that the speaker has stopped practicing scales and started a song.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The new commas slow the line, matching the moment the speaker finally plays smoothly.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The new commas slow the line, matching the moment the speaker finally plays smoothly.$q$, $q$The change comes in the same stanza where "one scale come[s] out smooth," so the slower, more careful line reflects that turning point. Thursday is when the speaker improves, not when the mistakes increase.$q$, 'draft', '87aa5ec6-ebf2-5a87-b76e-6e1b04448789')
