-- Passage rg7-literary-structure-pov-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('9ec32c02-5e39-5842-9343-86d9641f2b9d', 'rg7-literary-structure-pov-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Behind the Garage Door$q$, $q$Ever since my sister Noor turned sixteen, she has acted like I am invisible. I am not exaggerating. Every day after school, she disappears into the garage and shuts the door. When I knock, she yells, "Busy!" When I ask what she is doing, she says, "Nothing you'd care about."

Fine. I can be busy too.

On Tuesday, I noticed sawdust in her hair at dinner. Mom raised her eyebrows at Noor, and Noor shook her head very slightly. They both glanced at me and then looked away. Clearly they were talking about how annoying I am.

On Wednesday, Noor asked me, out of nowhere, how many books I own. I told her I had no idea, maybe sixty, and why did she care? She shrugged and wrote something on her hand. Then she asked if my favorite color was still green. I said it was, but that she would know that if she ever talked to me.

On Thursday, I heard a saw buzzing behind the garage door, and Dad's voice saying, "Measure twice, cut once." Even Dad gets invited in, I thought. Everyone but me.

My birthday is Saturday. I am not expecting much. Noor will probably give me a card she bought at the last minute, the way she did last year. I have decided I will not even care.

Still, on my way to bed tonight, I smelled fresh green paint coming from the garage.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
