   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A compost pile can look like a heap of trash. Earthworms and beetles live in it, and on cool mornings the pile sometimes gives off steam into the air.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"lists-minor-details"},{"text":"Composting is the smartest thing a family can do for the planet. Anyone who throws food in the trash is being wasteful and should start a compost pile right away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Bacteria, fungi and small creatures break down scraps in a compost pile. With a mix of materials, air and water, the pile heats up and becomes soil that helps gardens grow.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Greens such as fruit peels supply nitrogen, and browns such as dry leaves supply carbon. A gardener needs to add both kinds of material to a compost pile.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Bacteria, fungi and small creatures break down scraps in a compost pile. With a mix of materials, air and water, the pile heats up and becomes soil that helps gardens grow.$q$, $q$The first choice covers the workers, the conditions and the result without adding opinions. The second choice adds judgments such as "smartest" and "wasteful" that the passage never states.$q$, 'draft', '3d121767-9c86-5478-99a1-76c759eb12e4')
