   $q$Which detail from the passage shows that Keiko's first bridge design was not working?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Haru had folded a paper fan during his art class.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The new bridge held more than four hundred pennies.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-subject"},{"text":"It sagged in the middle every time before the cup was half full.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The science fair was going to take place on Friday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It sagged in the middle every time before the cup was half full.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says the bridge "sagged in the middle before the cup of pennies was even half full" all eleven times. The four hundred pennies describe the new bridge, not the first one.$q$, 'draft', 'd78c87b6-a0a8-50d7-8f3b-46367c0c07c7')
