   $q$The grandfather "asks me to say it twice." What does this detail most likely suggest about him?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He enjoys hearing the speaker shout across the yard.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He has forgotten how to read the numbers himself.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He does not trust the speaker to tell the truth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"He cares about writing each number down exactly right.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He cares about writing each number down exactly right.$q$, $q$He has kept a careful record for forty-one years because "Somebody has to remember," so repeating the number fits his concern for accuracy. Nothing in the poem suggests he doubts the speaker's honesty.$q$, 'draft', 'be2fd60d-5a7e-5a39-ba5c-6f1106f82e2e')
