   $q$Why does the speaker shout "Zero" even though the tube was empty?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker thinks a day with no rain is a new record.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"The speaker wants to prove that the rain gauge is broken.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The speaker is annoyed at having to do the chore every day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The speaker realizes that dry days belong in the record too.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker realizes that dry days belong in the record too.$q$, $q$Right before shouting, the speaker remembers "the dry Augusts lined up in his handwriting," which shows dry days were always recorded. The speaker "almost didn't bother," but that hesitation is overcome, not a sign of annoyance.$q$, 'draft', 'be2fd60d-5a7e-5a39-ba5c-6f1106f82e2e')
