-- Passage rg7-story-details-inference-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f2f1db87-f07b-501b-b9cf-9a3919486787', 'rg7-story-details-inference-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-story-details-inference'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Magpie and the Mole$q$, $q$A magpie lived at the top of a tall pine, and she was proud of her nest. All summer she gathered bright things: a silver button, a blue bottle cap, a bead that caught the sun like a drop of water. Each evening she counted them aloud so the whole forest could hear.

Below the pine, a mole was digging. He did not look up at the treasures, and he did not count anything aloud. Every morning he carried acorns and dry beech nuts into a deep room under the roots.

"You work in the dark like a beetle," the magpie called down one afternoon. "Come up and see something beautiful."

"I have seen the sun," said the mole. "It does not stay all year."

The magpie laughed and went back to polishing her button.

When the first hard frost came, the berries vanished from the bushes, and snow buried the seeds on the forest floor. The magpie searched for three days. On the fourth morning, she landed beside a small hole near the roots of her own tree and called down, quietly this time.

The mole came up blinking. He looked at her for a long moment. Then he went back down and returned with two acorns, which he set on the snow between them.

The magpie ate them slowly. That evening, she did not count her treasures. She sat at the edge of her nest and watched the hole beneath the pine until the stars came out.$q$, 'draft')
