  ('4498424c-9e41-5d7d-a104-e5e1954a4394', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-theme-summary'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A speaker rushes along a beach for shells, then learns from an aunt to sit still and watch a tide pool come alive.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A tiny silver fish flashes once in a tide pool and then swims out of view.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A silly child wastes a beach trip until a much smarter aunt finally teaches a lesson.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"A speaker and an aunt catch a crab and a fish and carry them home in a bucket.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A speaker rushes along a beach for shells, then learns from an aunt to sit still and watch a tide pool come alive.$q$, $q$The correct choice covers the beginning, the aunt's example and the change without judging anyone. Words like "silly" and "smarter" are opinions, so that choice is not objective.$q$, 'draft', '29de25e5-8e0c-5c59-bb0a-315239eaa221')
