   $q$How does the final stanza develop the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The light pockets show that the speaker is sad about having no shells.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"The speaker repeats the first stanza to show that nothing has changed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The speaker now repeats the aunt's stillness, showing the lesson has become a habit.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker decides never to visit the beach again after the first trip.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker now repeats the aunt's stillness, showing the lesson has become a habit.$q$, $q$"This time I sit beside the rock" echoes the aunt, and the waiting world shows the speaker values watching over collecting. The empty pockets are not sad; they show the speaker no longer needs to grab things.$q$, 'draft', '29de25e5-8e0c-5c59-bb0a-315239eaa221')
