   $q$Which statement best expresses the theme of the fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Friends should always share their food with one another.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"minor-detail-as-theme"},{"text":"Herons are better at catching fish than any other marsh bird.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Dry summers are hard on every animal that lives in a marsh.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Focusing only on what you lack can hide your own strengths from you.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Focusing only on what you lack can hide your own strengths from you.$q$, $q$Tamsin feels small while measuring others, then discovers her long legs and patience only when she stops comparing. Sharing fish happens in the story, but it is a detail, not the central message.$q$, 'draft', '05118b28-a66c-5255-ad20-ee042c6532b9')
