   $q$Which pair of details best shows how Soo-ah changes from the beginning of the story to the end?$q$, $q$[{"text":"At first the quiet tray is taller, and at the end the music tray is in the garage.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"At first she is \"sure\" of her idea, and at the end she has \"a list of new questions.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"At first she sets up two trays, and at the end a judge stops at her table.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"minor-detail"},{"text":"At first she records the temperature, and at the end she earns an honorable mention.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"partially-relevant"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$At first she is "sure" of her idea, and at the end she has "a list of new questions."$q$, $q$Moving from certainty to curiosity shows that honest results taught her to keep questioning. The trays and the judge are events, but they do not show how her thinking changes.$q$, 'draft', '6a36ddd6-d4a4-5460-81b9-8556965530dd')
