   $q$The Latin root aud means "hear." Who is the "audience" in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The people who came to listen to the band play","is_correct":true},{"text":"The large room where the concert was held","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-place-people"},{"text":"The family members who played in the band","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-performer-listener"},{"text":"The workers who planned to fix the leaking roof","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The people who came to listen to the band play$q$, $q$Aud means "hear," so the audience is the group that listens, and the passage shows them clapping along to every song. The band members made the music rather than listened to it.$q$, 'draft', '12004cef-d6f1-59ec-9cfd-ca9516613eb8')
