   $q$The words "benefit" and "benefactor" share the root bene, and the ending -factor means "one who does or makes." What does "benefactor" mean as it is used to describe Mr. Lindqvist?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A person who receives money raised at an event","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-giver-receiver"},{"text":"A person who performs music at a benefit event","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A person who does good by giving help or money","is_correct":true},{"text":"A person who is in charge of a community building","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A person who does good by giving help or money$q$, $q$A benefactor is "one who does good," which fits Mr. Lindqvist paying for the posters and chairs while asking for nothing in return. The tempting wrong answer reverses the roles, since he gave help instead of receiving it.$q$, 'draft', '12004cef-d6f1-59ec-9cfd-ca9516613eb8')
