  ('3c941684-f3bc-5adf-8aa1-e22e6815ef5e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The Greek root phon means "sound," and tele means "far." What do these word parts tell you about the "telephone" described in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It carried written letters over long distances","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"},{"text":"It carried pictures from one city to another","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"It recorded sounds to be played back much later","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-first-root"},{"text":"It carried sound, such as a voice, over long distances","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It carried sound, such as a voice, over long distances$q$, $q$Tele plus phon means "far sound," which matches the passage saying the telephone "sent the human voice." Written letters fit the telegraph, which uses graph instead of phon.$q$, 'draft', '8b40a0a8-dbf0-598f-8321-e207b978a0c5')
