  ('8299c774-52a4-5959-9f2b-891fd5235891', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-word-parts'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The prefix con- means "together," and the Latin root struct means "build." What do beavers do when they "construct dams"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They search for dams that other animals made","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"They swim across dams to reach the pond","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"They build dams by putting materials together","is_correct":true},{"text":"They tear dams down to let the water flow","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They build dams by putting materials together$q$, $q$Con plus struct means "build together," and the passage describes beavers dragging logs and packing mud into place. Tearing dams down is the opposite of constructing them.$q$, 'draft', 'f900845c-2d04-5c22-b373-d9d6cbcf6f9c')
