   $q$The prefix sub- means "under," and merge comes from a Latin word meaning "to dip or plunge." Where are the lodge's entrances if they are "submerged"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Hidden behind a pile of loose sticks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Next to the shore where plants grow","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"Under the surface of the water","is_correct":true},{"text":"High above the surface of the water","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Under the surface of the water$q$, $q$Sub plus merge means "plunged under," and the passage says the entrances are "below the water's surface." The dry room is above the water, which may make the second choice tempting, but that describes a different part of the lodge.$q$, 'draft', 'f900845c-2d04-5c22-b373-d9d6cbcf6f9c')
