   $q$The root struct means "build." What does the word "structure" mean in the sentence about the lodge?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The way the lodge is built and arranged","is_correct":true},{"text":"The color and texture of the lodge's sticks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The number of years the lodge has stood","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The family of beavers living in the lodge","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-place-people"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The way the lodge is built and arranged$q$, $q$A structure is something built, or the way it is put together, and the passage explains how the entrances and dry room are planned. The sticks are part of the lodge, but their color is not what "carefully planned" refers to.$q$, 'draft', 'f900845c-2d04-5c22-b373-d9d6cbcf6f9c')
