  ('0be43cd2-3621-503c-9116-af4d23d2184e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The Greek root bio means "life," and the ending -logist means "one who studies." Who are the "biologists" in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Scientists who study living things","is_correct":true},{"text":"Scientists who study rocks and soil","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-root-meaning"},{"text":"Scientists who study weather and rain","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"Workers who build pipes through dams","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Scientists who study living things$q$, $q$Bio plus logist means "one who studies life," and the biologists in the passage study beavers and the plants and animals in their ponds. Someone who studies rocks and soil would be a geologist.$q$, 'draft', 'f900845c-2d04-5c22-b373-d9d6cbcf6f9c')
