  ('6c53f348-c4e1-57d9-b470-de0426fdce17', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The Greek root micro means "small," and scope means "look at." The passage mentions a "microscope." Based on these roots, which sentence uses the related word "microscopic" correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The beavers were microscopic about their dam, so they checked it every night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"The pond water held microscopic creatures that could be seen only through a lens.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The flood was microscopic, so it covered the road and the farm fields.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"The beaver lodge looked microscopic from the shore because it was so huge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The pond water held microscopic creatures that could be seen only through a lens.$q$, $q$Microscopic means so small that you need a lens to look at it, which fits tiny creatures in pond water. Using it for a huge lodge reverses the meaning of micro, and using it to mean "careful" confuses it with a different idea.$q$, 'draft', 'f900845c-2d04-5c22-b373-d9d6cbcf6f9c')
