   $q$The prefix per- means "through," and spect means "look." What is "perspective" in this passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A way of drawing that makes things seem near or far","is_correct":true},{"text":"A person's opinion about someone from the past","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-sense-of-word"},{"text":"A way of choosing bright colors for a background","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A way of measuring how tall a brick wall is","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A way of drawing that makes things seem near or far$q$, $q$Perspective is about how things look to a viewer, and the passage shows Keiko making the road seem to stretch "far into the distance." Perspective can also mean a point of view or opinion, but that sense does not fit a sentence about drawing lines.$q$, 'draft', 'edb3f6fa-e5cf-5542-ad86-5cf94ab240ca')
