   $q$Which statement best evaluates the author's claim that small fields "will also make players enjoy the game more, so fewer of them will quit"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is well supported, because the touch counts prove that players are happier on small fields.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overreads-evidence"},{"text":"It is unsupported, because the passage gives no survey or quit rates, and touch counts measure activity, not enjoyment.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is unsupported, because the passage says that players dislike small fields.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It is well supported, because Tomas kept playing until high school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is unsupported, because the passage gives no survey or quit rates, and touch counts measure activity, not enjoyment.$q$, $q$The author offers no data about enjoyment or quitting, so the claim rests on a guess. The touch counts show more activity, but more touches do not prove that players feel happier.$q$, 'draft', '891e9a60-08d6-552e-9a3b-cd23a10a8534')
